  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 122 PM CDT Tue Jun 30 2026\n\nJune nears the end, with near steady temperatures and heat indices \nof 100-108 persisting daily into early next week. Meanwhile, a large \nhigh pressure system over the eastern US will continue to dominate, \nnot moving much until the latter half of this week.\n\nMultiple shortwaves will weaken the ridge to end the work week, \nenhancing moisture across South Texas with PWATs between 1.75- 2.0\". \nThis moisture and seabreeze will bring daily very low rain chances. \nZooming into early next week, the synoptic flow becomes uncertain.\n\nRecent model runs have trended towards a more zonal flow, with \nensemble guidance still varying widely. The GEFS/CMC ensembles favor \ntaller heights at 500mb over the northern CONUS, whereas the ENS \nindicates shorter heights (troughing). However, deterministic runs \nresult in either a mid-level trough digging into S TX or cut-off low \nentering Mexico. Both scenarios warrant very low rain chances to \ndwell into early next week.\n\n\"Signing off after 34 years of federal service. Be safe everyone!\"\nThank you, John! Enjoy your retirement!",
